    "synopsis": {
        "native": "Une association accueille des jeunes LGBT mis \u00e0 la rue par leurs familles. Derri\u00e8re l\u2019apparente com\u00e9die, les exc\u00e8s, l\u2019envie de s'affirmer, se cachent des vies bris\u00e9es. Tous ont cette furieuse envie d\u2019exister, de trouver leur place dans la soci\u00e9t\u00e9. Ici, ils ont six mois, pour trouver un travail, un logement et s\u2019accepter comme ils sont. Une course contre la montre durant laquelle No\u00eblle (Val\u00e9rie Lemercier) qui dirige l\u2019association et Alex (Finnegan Oldfield), qui s\u2019y retrouve contre son gr\u00e9, sont \u00e9galement renvoy\u00e9s \u00e0 leurs propres failles et s\u2019interrogent sur leurs motivations \u00e0 aider les autres.",
        "english": "Navigating the delicate balance between who they really are and their thirst for acceptance and love, a diverse group of LGBT youths rescued from the street have only six months! A painfully short amount of time to find a job, a place to live and a way to self-acceptance. They can\u2019t stay any longer, the waiting lists are just too long\u2026 Struggling to stay out of trouble, estranged from his family, Alex has committed yet another petty crime and is assigned by his parole officer, to serve the community by working at the LGBT shelter for a month. Initially very reluctant, Alex can\u2019t help but get attached to the damaged yet exceptional and endearing youths he encounters at the shelter. All the shelter\u2019s volunteers and social workers must themselves battle their own flaws and sometimes even question their motivations for helping others\u2026 Alex comes to terms with the brutal fact that they just can\u2019t rescue everyone. But if all they can save is a single life, it\u2019s all worth it\u2026"
    },
